# CQ-13 · trait-bundle-agentive-count
#
# Question: Which entities in the corpus are both Agentive and Count — the
#           things that can act and can be counted one by one?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. The trait bundle replaces
#           the v0.1 Object/Item/Unique split, and this is the query that asks
#           whether the replacement can express the distinction it removed.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §3.2 (trait-bundle entity model); §5.4; §5.12
# Form:     SELECT — one row per entity
# Note:     `vso:class` is OPTIONAL because the two class idioms of §5.4 are
#           both conformant: the Penman transpiler compiles a bareword to a
#           `vso:class` IRI, while `examples/throne_room.ttl` types its entities
#           with `rdf:type` into a document-local taxonomy. An UNBOUND class in
#           this answer is the second idiom, not a missing value.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?entity ?class
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?entity vso:animacy vso:Agentive ; vso:countability vso:Count .
    OPTIONAL { ?entity vso:class ?class }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?entity
